      "actual_outcome_target_in_T": false,
      "clause_id": "DR-019",
      "end_character": 533,
      "excerpt": "A Derived Refresh is the deterministic regeneration and validation of a noncanonical projection from an unchanged canonical machine input under an exact generator binding. It records the canonical input digest, generator identity and digest, output digest, parity result, and validation receipt. A Derived Refresh creates no Semantic Epoch, Representation Revision, Governance Decision, or authority effect. A change to the generator is governed separately as a tooling change even when refreshing its outputs has no semantic effect.",
